    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d912">

                <pb facs="0950" n="942" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg942"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.6354/67: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-20T18:00:00+01:00">June 20, 1938—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 20—1:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>537. Todd states International Tin Committee accepted buffer stock scheme with
                    only slight modification.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d912-f1"/> He made formal
                    objection regarding price pegging and also the height of the price range. It
                    would appear that he conducted himself ably.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d912-f1" n="7" xml:id="d912-f1-content">
                <p>For text of the agreement, signed June 20, 1938, see British Cmd. 5879: <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Papers Relating to the International Tin Control
                        Scheme</hi>, p. 12.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
